Build approach
--------------
Use KDE Builder with a separate installation prefix and the existing user
account. The distro Plasma session remains the fallback. Do not replace
system graphics libraries or force a running desktop restart.
The configuration is a build starting point, not a complete dependency installer.
Supporting Plasma components use Plasma/6.7 for compatibility with Qt 6.10.
Frameworks currently track latest-kf6, so they are not yet reproducibly pinned.
Wayland 1.26.0 and wayland-protocols 1.49 are built in the separate prefix.
KWin retains the experimental revision above; compatibility still needs testing.

Planned verification
--------------------
Verify installed binaries, linked libraries and development login selection.
Confirm normal Plasma remains selectable and accessible.
Test per-output GPU assignment, desktop responsiveness and OBS recording.
Start with DisplayLink outputs disabled for the initial controlled test.
Record failures and limitations rather than claiming all visual hangs are fixed.

Recovery
--------
A complete recovery procedure will be added after the actual login-session
entry and launch environment have been installed and checked.
